# Tier boundary for ~/.emacs.d
#
# This directory is a git worktree that Emacs ALSO WRITES TO: history files,
# completion caches, byte-compiled code, downloaded language servers. The old
# scheme tried to name each generated file in the repo's root .gitignore and
# lost - 915 of 924 tracked files here are vendored elpa, and runtime state
# kept slipping in. So the rule is inverted:
#
#     authored files are re-included below; anything not listed is junk by design.
#
# The pattern MUST stay `/*` (anchored, so it matches depth-1 entries only).
# A bare `*` has no separator, and an unanchored pattern matches at EVERY depth
# - then `!lisp/` re-includes only the directory and every .el inside it is
# silently ignored. Verified: with bare `*`, `git check-ignore -q lisp/packages.el`
# reports IGNORED. Do not change `/*` to `*`, `*/` or `**` either.
#
# To version a new authored file here: add a `!` line below, then run
# tests/emacs-test. Add the `!` in the same commit that adds the file - no
# speculative entries (notably no `!init.el`: package.el and customize can
# both CREATE an init file, so a speculative entry is a permanent hole).
#
# Canonical clone: ~/prog/dotfiles. Other hosts may still track the files this
# one no longer does.
/*

# .gitignore MUST be re-included: an ignore file works whether or not it is
# tracked, so if `/*` swallowed this one, these rules would keep working on the
# host that wrote them and silently not exist anywhere else.
!.gitignore

# Symlink to ../.emacs, kept as the find-user-init-file fallback. It is inert
# while init always symlinks ~/.emacs, and costs nothing. This was argued and
# kept deliberately - do not delete the line as "unused".
!.emacs

# Re-included before the draft lands, so the day early-init.el is added it is
# not silently ignored.
!early-init.el

!.dir-locals.el

# Authored elisp. Re-including the directory is what lets git descend into it.
!lisp/

# Re-include the directory, then exclude its contents, then re-include the one
# file worth keeping. Collapsing `transient/*` + `!transient/history.el` into
# `!transient/` re-admits transient/session-* - same parent-directory rule as
# `/*` above, one level down.
!transient/
transient/*
!transient/history.el

# elpa/ is a depth-1 entry, so `/*` ALREADY matches it. It stays tracked pending
# `git rm -r --cached .emacs.d/elpa`; gitignore never untracks, so until then
# edits to elpa files still show in `git status` while NEW files inside it do
# not. This file is not incomplete - adding a rule here does nothing on its own.
